{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall proclaim on the very day, a holy convocation.</b> That Scripture did not specify in which month and on what day this festival falls, as it specified for the other appointed times — this is the reason: had it specified its time, we would not count the seven weeks; rather, we would rely to observe the festival at its stated time, and a great matter depends on our counting, as stated above. But now that we count the seven weeks from the time of the omer harvest, it automatically follows that the fiftieth day falls on the sixth of Sivan, which is the day of the giving of the Ten Commandments. And since the count of fifty days is only for the purpose of Atzeret, the bringing of the omer is not called a time for reciting Shehecheyanu over it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:37.646454880Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}